# Architecture Plan

## Product Scope

The app is a single-page email sender. Issue #19 makes its background much
more vivid and guarantees the color treatment fills the entire browser
viewport, including areas outside the page content.

## Module Structure

- `src/client/App.tsx`: email composer markup and client-side form state.
- `src/client/styles.css`: global canvas, responsive layout, component styling,
  and the full-page layered gradient for issue #19.
- `src/client/main.tsx`: client bootstrap and stylesheet import.
- `src/client/sendEmail.ts`: same-origin send endpoint client.
- `src/shared/email.ts`: request and response types shared with the server.
- `src/server/`: Express app, send route, and email provider adapter.
- `tests/`: endpoint, provider, and end-to-end send-flow coverage.

## Issue Dependencies

1. Issue #19 depends only on the existing client stylesheet and root page
   structure.
2. It has no dependencies on email delivery, shared types, persistence, or
   server configuration.

## Key Design Decisions

- Apply the background to the actual document canvas (`html`, `body`, and app
  root sizing) rather than relying solely on `:root`, so it remains visible
  across the full viewport and during content overflow.
- Use a high-saturation base gradient with multiple radial color blooms for a
  visibly colorful result at common desktop and mobile aspect ratios.
- Keep the composer and form surfaces sufficiently opaque and preserve dark
  foreground colors to protect contrast and usability.
- Keep the implementation CSS-only; no changes are needed to form behavior,
  API contracts, or server code.
